.TH TOS_EXTRACT_SPRITES 1
.SH NAME
tos_extract_sprites, tos_extract_bitmaps, tos_expand \- recover TempleOS sprites and sources for Inferno
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 scripts/tos_expand.py
.I iso
.B -o
.I outdir
[
.B -v
]
.PP
.B python3 scripts/tos_extract_sprites.py
.I file
.B -o
.I outdir
[
.B --prefix
.I name
]
[
.B --spr
.I dir
]
.PP
.B python3 scripts/tos_extract_bitmaps.py
.I file
.B -o
.I outdir
[
.B --prefix
.I name
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are host Python programs (not Dis modules) used to carry
TempleOS art into this tree.
.PP
.I Tos_expand
reads a TempleOS distribution ISO, walks its RedSea filesystem, and
writes every file into
.IR outdir ,
expanding TempleOS's own LZW-style
.B .Z
compression as it goes.
It exists because the TempleOS source mirrors circulating on the web
passed through an export that stripped every 0x05 byte, silently
corrupting the binary DolDoc sprite records embedded in
.B .HC
files; the ISO is the only faithful source.
(Stripping the 0x05 bytes from a file it writes reproduces the
mirrored copy byte for byte, which is how the corruption was
diagnosed.)
.PP
.I Tos_extract_sprites
reads a DolDoc file, walks its binary sprite bins, and
.I rasterizes
each one at 1:1 scale the way
.B GrSpritePlot
would draw it: colors, dithers, thickness, lines, arrows, rectangles,
circles, ellipses, regular polygons, polylines, B-splines, flood
fills, embedded bitmaps, planar symmetry, shifts, and text in the
authentic 8x8 system font.
For each bin it writes an
.B m8
.B .bit
and a
.B k1
.B .mask
named
.IB prefix _ binnum ,
with the image rectangle placed so that the sprite's origin is (0,0)
\(em drawing the image through its mask at point
.I p
puts the sprite where TempleOS's
.B Sprite(dc,x,y)
would.
Mesh bins are 3D and are skipped (see
.B scripts/tos_extract_meshes.py ).
With
.B --spr
it also dumps each bin's element list as one-line-per-element text,
for tools that want the vectors rather than a raster.
.PP
.I Tos_extract_bitmaps
is the older, simpler tool: it converts only
.B SPT_BITMAP
records and ignores vector elements.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /icons/temple/*.bit
rasterized sprites, named
.IB app _ binnum
.TP
.B /lib/temple/sprites/*.spr
element-list dumps
.TP
.B /fonts/temple/temple.font
the TempleOS 8x8 system font, generated from
.B Kernel/FontStd.HC
.SH SOURCE
.B /scripts/tos_expand.py
.br
.B /scripts/tos_extract_sprites.py
.br
.B /scripts/tos_extract_bitmaps.py
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR image (6),
.IR draw-image (2)
.SH BUGS
Flood fills are rasterized on the sprite's own transparent canvas, so
a fill that in TempleOS would spill onto surrounding screen pixels is
clipped to the sprite's bounding box instead.
B-splines are sampled uniformly rather than with TempleOS's exact
stepping, so a curve can differ by a pixel.
